    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nDisplay of virtual lines with `virt_lines_overflow = 'wrap'` does not respect 'linebreak' option. I.e. virtual lines always wrap as if 'linebreak' is disabled.\n\nHere is an example repro:\n\n```lua\nlocal line = string.rep('word ', 100)\nvim.api.nvim_buf_set_lines(0, 0, -1, false, { line })\n\nlocal ns_id = vim.api.nvim_create_namespace('test')\nlocal extmark_opts = { virt_lines_overflow = 'wrap', virt_lines = { { { line, 'String' } } } }\nvim.api.nvim_buf_set_extmark(0, ns_id, 0, 0, extmark_opts)\n\nvim.wo.linebreak = true\n```\n\nAnd here is how it looks:\n\n<img width=\"2880\" height=\"1734\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bbdd2cf7-17ab-4262-a63f-93bea4a6f3b5\" />\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nWrapping of virtual lines with `virt_lines_overflow = 'wrap'` (and `'auto'` with enabled 'wrap') respects the 'linebreak' (and by continuation 'breakat') options.\n\nIn particular case of the repro, both buffer and virtual line should wrap exactly the same.",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
